   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "מַתְחִיל בִּגְנוּת וּמְסַיֵּים בְּשֶׁבַח. מַאי בִּגְנוּת? רַב אָמַר: ״מִתְּחִלָּה עוֹבְדֵי עֲבוֹדָה זָרָה הָיוּ אֲבוֹתֵינוּ״. [וּשְׁמוּאֵל] אָמַר: ״עֲבָדִים הָיִינוּ״.",
   "en": "It was taught in the mishna that the father «begins» his answer «with disgrace and concludes with glory.» The Gemara asks: «What» is the meaning of the term: «With disgrace? Rav said» that one should begin by saying: «At first our forefathers were idol worshippers,» before concluding with words of glory. «And Shmuel said:» The disgrace with which one should begin his answer is: «We were slaves.»"
  }
